   "claims": [
    "The score is based on performance in two sections, each contributing 50% of the total score: Multiple-choice section — 60 questions.",
    "The College Board combines the results to produce the final AP® score, reported on a 1-5 scale.",
    "Each section contributes 50% to your final score, and you need to scale it to a maximum of 120 points.",
    "You can apply the following formula: MCQ + FRQ × 60/36 Use the AP® Bio score breakdown table to find the result in the scale from 1 to 5.",
    "In 2025, the average AP® Bio score was 3.2.",
    "In previous years, the mean score typically hovered around 2.9, making 2025 a relatively strong year for test-takers.",
    "For a deeper look at historical trends, the College Board publishes the AP® Biology score distribution every year since 2002.",
    "The built-in AP® Biology score conversion chart​ finds your composite score and projected final score on the 1-5 scale automatically.",
    "Yes, a 4 on the AP® Biology score is considered strong.",
    "The official College Board recommendation is well qualified for this score, since only approximately 40% of students earn a 4 or 5 on the AP® Bio exam."
   ],
